Jahshaka patch 0053 — setSky() records the method it was given.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this. `OgreMain/src/OgreSceneManager.cpp` is also touched by patch 0016
(`_warmUpShadersCollect`), far from this hunk; the two apply in stack order.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT A WORKAROUND (owner rule, 2026-09-15, ledger §325; audit
SPECS/audits/ENGINE_WORKAROUNDS_TO_PATCHES_2026-09-15.md finding F14).
`SceneManager::mSkyMethod` is assigned in the CONSTRUCTOR and nowhere else:
`setSky( bEnabled, skyMethod, texture )` uses its argument to pick the material
and to validate the texture type, and never stores it. So
`SceneManager::getSkyMethod()` answers `SkyCubemap` for the life of the scene
manager, whatever sky is actually up — a getter that cannot be used for
anything, including the round trip that turning the sky off reads as
(`setSky( false, getSkyMethod(), … )`, which is what upstream's own API shape
invites).

The engine kept its own `bool mSkyIsEquirect` beside the sky it had set, in
three writes and one read, because the engine's equirect sky needs a WRAPPED u
axis on the sampler (a lat-long image's left and right edges are the same
meridian; `Sky.material` clamps both axes) and a cube sky must not get it. That
mirror is deleted with this patch: the engine asks the SceneManager what its
sky is.

No picture changes anywhere: the assignment feeds one getter nothing upstream
reads.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin and `git apply
--reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh` re-run in the lane worktree;
`--engine-selftest` byte-identical (`b55e2d5d…`) — the default scene's sky is
the colour sky. The behavioural gate is the sky suites (`sky.*`,
`gi.probe_sky`, `scripting.e2e.sky*`), which cover both methods and the
equirect seam.

--- a/OgreMain/src/OgreSceneManager.cpp
+++ b/OgreMain/src/OgreSceneManager.cpp
@@ -1081,6 +1081,13 @@
 
         if( bEnabled )
         {
+            // The method the sky is actually using. getSkyMethod() used to report the
+            // constructor's SkyCubemap for the life of the SceneManager no matter what
+            // was set here, so it could not be used for anything -- including the
+            // round trip setSky( false, getSkyMethod(), ... ) that turning the sky off
+            // reads as.
+            mSkyMethod = skyMethod;
+
             if( !mSky )
             {
                 mSky = createRectangle2D( SCENE_STATIC );
